From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gpu31-mesa <gpu31-mesa@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] panfrost: v5.2 UAPI compatibility (GPU_PROD_ID + SUBMIT +
 v52-selftest)

The T720 bring-up kernel implements the Linux v5.2 panfrost UAPI
(gpu31-target.md H1: 6 ioctls 0x00-0x05; GET_PARAM answers only
GPU_PROD_ID; SUBMIT ends at `requirements`; CREATE_BO.flags
reserved-zero; verified byte-identical to refs/tags/v5.2 14817897).
Mesa 27.0.0-devel speaks a 14-ioctl superset (MADVISE/SYNC_BO/
QUERY_BO_INFO/SET_LABEL/JM_CTX_*/PERFCNT + 40 GET_PARAMs + wider
SUBMIT) and fails closed (assert/abort) on the first probe the v5.2
kernel answers -EINVAL to.  This patch adds a small compat shim behind
the existing ops hooks (panfrost_kmod_dev.ops.get_param/submit_job +
pan_kmod_ops.submit_job, all introduced by 0001/0002) so the stock
DRM backend runs unchanged on v5.2:

- GET_PARAM (panfrost_kmod_v52_get_param): only GPU_PROD_ID ever hits
  the kernel.  Everything else is answered from the live T720 capture
  in docs/reports/gpu-verify.md (GPU_ID 0x07201000, shader 0x3/2
  cores, tiler 1, l2 1, mem 1, mmu 0x2821/VA33, l2 0x07110206, tiler
  0x809, thread 0x0a040400/256-core, js 0x7, single group, coherency
  NONE, prios MEDIUM-only, timestamp 0/no-frequency) plus the same
  arch-based thread fallbacks panfrost_kmod.c already uses, so the
  decode matches either way.  Signature: (dev, get_param) to match
  the ops.get_param hook.  Units (Hz vs MHz, ns vs cycles) follow
  mainline call sites: values that only feed multiplication/division
  in driver code are returned in mainline units (frequencies in Hz,
  timestamps in ns); opaque bitmasks pass through untouched.
- SUBMIT (panfrost_kmod_v52_submit): strips the post-v5.2 tail before
  the ioctl (jm_ctx_handle/pad never sent: v5.2 struct is 8 bytes
  shorter and the tail would alias bo_handles/bo_handle_count on the
  kernel side), rejects non-FS requirements exactly like v5.2's
  panfrost_ioctl_submit (PANFROST_JD_REQ_FS allowed,
  PANFROST_JD_REQ_CYCLE_COUNT tolerated-with-warning because the
  kernel-side requirement check predates it and drops it nowhere),
  and passes the trimmed struct (all fields up to `requirements`
  copied, jm_ctx_handle/pad dropped) to the v5.2 SUBMIT number.
- No-op stubs for post-v5.2 ioctls: WAIT_BO (real ioctl, present in
  v5.2), SYNC_BO flush (ret 0, queue drained), MADVISE evict (no-op) /
  unevictable (true: backing store always exists), SET_LABEL_BO
  (no-op), QUERY_BO_INFO import path (GET_BO_OFFSET only, no cached
  flags), PERFCNT create/enable/disable/dump (ENOSYS + preserve the
  unstable_ioctls hint), timestamp query (0: no SYSTEM_TIMESTAMP on
  v5.2).
- THREAD feature decode: not all kernels answer THREAD_FEATURES, so
  the shim decodes max_tasks_per_core / num_registers_per_core from
  the T720-known 0x0a040400 exactly the way panfrost_kmod.c does
  (top byte, low 16 bits), falling back to the arch defaults.

Three files:

- src/panfrost/lib/kmod/panfrost_kmod_v52_compat.h: the shim
  (static-inline, internal linkage, no new exported symbols).
- src/panfrost/lib/kmod/panfrost_kmod.c: route get_param + submit_job
  through the shim (two call-site swaps; hook tables untouched).
- src/panfrost/lib/kmod/panfrost_kmod_v52_selftest.c: host test
  (T720 GPU_ID decode, submit trimming, requirement gate, no
  post-v5.2 ioctl numbers) wired to meson `meson test v52-compat`.

Out of scope: JM_CTX_CREATE/DESTROY are never issued on the v5.2 DRM
backend (0002 only calls the direct ioctl when ops->jm_ctx_create is
NULL AND the fd is not the default context; T720 uses the default
context, handle 0, so no new ioctl row is needed).  The v5.2 CREATE_BO
flags==0 rule lives in the kernel (returns -EINVAL on nonzero), not
here: to_panfrost_bo_flags() already maps heap->0 for this path.
